with relevance  and just do a a custom range for  whatever time period i'm looking for  if you're looking for patents you can  find them too in this case i'm not  looking for patents  what i also think is interesting  and useful is that you can  limit your search to review articles now  what are review articles review articles  are where the authors have taken all of  the available knowledge  from many different scientific articles  and sort of distilled it down and  summarized it into one  review  so this is sometimes called a literature  review  and so a lot of these right here may be  review articles or and you can see  there's many pages of hits here  or they might be  scientific articles where there was an  actual experiment right so an experiment  was conducted and the results of that  single experiment are being uh reported  but if you just want the review articles  basically the summaries then you can  then you can hit that review articles  and this is a great way to learn about a  topic that you don't know much about and  then you can go back to any type if you  are looking for more about  specific experiments that have been  published on  you can also create an alert so to  create an alert all you do is click here  and any time a new  anytime a new article is published and  is added to the google scholar database  then uh  if if it would show up in this in this  inquiry in this uh type of search term  then you can have it emailed to yourself  so you just hit create alert it's got  your email address right there  and you hit create alert and then you  can get email alerts whenever  new  articles about catridiomycosis and  temporanes come out for example  a few other things i want to point out  here  so we've got the title and of course you  can click on this i'm going to right  click and open in a new tab just to show  you what that looks like so i can go to  the basically the publisher's website  in this case it says purchase pdf  or i can access it through my  institution so you know not all of these  will be free  if you need something and you don't want  to pay for it sometimes you can email  the author get the email address right  here  and ask them to share the pdf with you  or you can go through an interlibrary  loan process  now if i go back to here you can see  you've also got the first few authors um  the date that's the the first few words  of the journal  and then a few things down here so  what's this star this star is to save  something so if i save it you can see it  says save to your library now i can come  over here and click on my library and  see all of the articles that i have  starred from various searches that's  just a way to save articles in one place  that are of interest to you  you can also click on this quotation  mark and this is going to give you  different types of citations so you can  just click usually i use apa i can click  on that i can do you know ctrl c to copy  it  or right click to copy if you don't want  to use the keyboard shortcuts and then i  can paste that into whatever document  i'm working on into my references or  works cited section if you use various  uh you know reference citation programs  you can get  links to those down here and then import  the citation into your program that you  use you can also see this is cited by 34  this means 34 other  scientific  papers  have cited this one  so you can kind of see like this one  cited by a hundred and fifty three this  is probably an important article in this  field  this one um doesn't seem to have been  cited by anyone yet of course it is just  a recent publication so maybe that's why  this one is a little bit older i'm only  cited by one so it might be a little bit  more niche or a little bit  you know a little bit more specific or  or less important to the field  so you can use that as kind of a measure  to find  the most cited papers in a field also if  you know you're interested in this paper  you can click on cited 